From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0790: render target pipelines kept across runs: the keys of the ownership transfer and dump pipelines go to <title>.rtv.d3d12.xrtp and their pipelines are made at start

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (pipeline-cache diagnosis of 2026-11-27, scratch/pipeline-cache/DIAGNOSIS.md)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: About 200 of the D3D12 pipelines a run counts in rexgpu_pipeline_creations are the render target cache's ownership transfer
  pipelines (D3D12RenderTargetCache::GetOrCreateTransferPipelines: 1 per TransferShaderKey, 8 stencil-bit ones + 1 on a GPU without
  pixel-shader stencil reference) and its dump pipelines. They were never stored, so every process made them again on the command
  processor thread in the first frames of each scene (the 115-205 ms front-end hitches). The key of each one made on first use is
  appended (and flushed: a few dozen records a run, the process ends with _Exit) to <cache>/shaders/shareable/<title>.rtv.d3d12.xrtp
  (12-byte header: 'XRTP', version 1, context = use_stencil_reference_output, depth_transfer_not_equal_test, msaa_2x_supported, the
  number of transfer modes; a mismatching file is dropped and made again; then 8-byte records: kind 1 = TransferShaderKey, 2 =
  DumpPipelineKey, and the key). D3D12CommandProcessor::InitializeShaderStorage calls
  D3D12RenderTargetCache::InitializeRuntimePipelineStorage after the draw pipelines' preload, which makes the stored keys' pipelines on
  the command processor thread at start (not counted as run-time creations) and logs "Created N render target pipelines for K ownership
  transfer and M dump keys from the storage in X milliseconds (F failed, R rejected)". The first run with no file hitches as before.
  No cvar. Needs the series up to 0590 (the counter it keeps out of).
  Validated 2026-11-27 (RTX 4060 laptop, 1080p quick_drive, shared cache): run b-a1 (no .xrtp): 197 run-time creations, all of them
  render target transfer pipelines (windows 9 / 120 / 41 / 27, made in 1 / 17 / 4 / 3 ms: 0.14 ms each), 0 for draws, the file is
  556 bytes = 12 + 68 keys. Warm runs b-b1..b-b3: 'Created 201 render target pipelines for 64 ownership transfer and 4 dump
  keys from the storage in 21 milliseconds (0 failed, 0 rejected)', 0 run-time creations, '[mcla-hitch] ... pipelines +0'; a new key
  met later (b-f2) is appended (68 -> 72 keys) and made at the next start. The front end's worst frame: 148.5 ms (b-a1) ->
  131.6 / 132.0 / 95.6 ms warm: the pipelines were 25 ms of it, not the 45-115 ms estimated; the rest is page faults (see the host's
  mcla_prefault_guest, src/host/pf_probe.h) and D3D12 resource creation.
Bucket: REDO

0790-render-target-pipeline-keys.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, T0/T2).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h
